<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŭres</span></b> , ium, m.
		(parvi, <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
			2, 135</span></i>) and f. (Tatiae, <i><span class="en">Prop. 5, 9,
		74</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύρεις</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύρις</span> [curis, Sabine word, = hasta, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
		477</span></i>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				ancient chief town of the Sabines</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 51</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 15, 20, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
				811</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 638</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				14, 778 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 13, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 18, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1, 2,
				1</span></i>; cf. Quirites.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>the inhabitants of
				Cures</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3, 201</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6,
			216</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŭren-sis</span></b> ,
				e, <i>adj., of Cures</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 94</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŭrenses</span></b> , ium, m.,
				<i>the inhabitants of Cures</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 68</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 12, 17, §
			107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŭrētis</span></b> ,
				is (or perh. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŭres</span></b> , ētis), m., <i>an inhabitant of Cures</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i>
			(5), 4, 9.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
